WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.730
Two closed books.

2
00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:04.060
No titles, no covers.

3
00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:06.450
One is labelled 1818.

4
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:09.130
The other, 1898.

5
00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.890
Over the first, a candle gutters.

6
00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:16.540
Over the second, a microscope
appears, then slowly turns,

7
00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:19.480
until its lens is pointing back at you.

8
00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:22.800
The second book imagines
minds watching us:

9
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:26.980
"intellects vast and
cool and unsympathetic".

10
00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:29.080
Both novels are about science.

11
00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:30.290
So what?

12
00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:33.620
What kind of connection
actually earns the marks?

13
00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:37.570
In this mission, you'll see
what AO4 actually asks of you,

14
00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.250
in its own words.

15
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:43.460
You'll find both novels opening a
key scene with an act of looking.

16
00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:48.810
And you'll sort possible connections, and
decide which ones an examiner rewards.

17
00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:52.520
Your mission: work out what
kind of connection scores.
